From 44361c42ea7267fcc0999569b314d6b957cded76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patch Baseline <patch@local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 21:20:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(homepage): build real bilingual marketing homepage, move
 app pages behind a route group
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Previously '/' just did a hard redirect to /dashboard — there was no
public-facing page at all, and the app's logged-in Navbar (including a
publicly-reachable Admin link) rendered on every page since it lived in
the root layout.

Homepage:
- Real marketing page: hero, feature rows, 'designed for real routines'
  section, an insight teaser, an FAQ accordion, and a footer
- Bangla/English toggle, defaulting to Bangla, persisted via localStorage
- Copy is written to be genuinely attention-grabbing (curiosity-driven
  headlines, direct CTAs) without fabricating fake user counts, fake
  testimonials, or countdown urgency
- CTA honestly says 'Try It Now' and routes to /onboarding (free) rather
  than 'Subscribe', since Bdapps billing isn't wired up yet — trivial to
  relabel once it is
- Self-hosted Bengali fonts (@fontsource/noto-sans-bengali,
  @fontsource/noto-serif-bengali) instead of next/font/google, so the
  build has no dependency on reaching Google's font CDN at build time —
  more robust for a shared-hosting deployment target

Routing:
- dashboard/tracker/plan/progress/admin/onboarding moved into an
  app/(app)/ route group with their own layout carrying the Navbar and
  food search modal — URLs are unchanged, but the marketing homepage no
  longer inherits the logged-in app chrome (including the previously
  publicly-exposed Admin nav link)
- Moved pages' imports switched from relative paths to the existing @/
  alias, which is more robust than relative-path depth counting if the
  folder structure changes again later

Verified: full workspace build + real 'next build' production build +
all 7 routes return 200 + all 80 existing tests still pass + rendered
homepage HTML confirmed to contain zero external font domain references.
